      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Residual knowledge typically refers to the methods and skills you acquire, which are not specific proprietary details but rather generalized techniques or concepts you learn during your work. A very specific way to optimize a proprietary database architecture could still be considered confidential if it's uniquely tied to the client's specific systems or technologies. It's wise to err on the side of caution. Always check the NDA's definition of \"residual\" or consider consulting with a legal professional to clarify before applying any learned techniques to other projects, especially if they closely resemble proprietary knowledge of your current or any previous clients.",
