    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i guess it's a fine line. basically, if i can do it without using their actual data or specific code, i should be fine. but what if the \"trick\" is so specific that anyone who sees it would immediately know it came from their system? is there a way to frame it as a \"general skill\" when i'm explaining my workflow to future clients? I want to be able to talk about my expertise without sounding like i'm leaking secrets.",
