      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, framing advanced techniques as general skills that were honed through your professional experience is a common approach. When discussing your expertise, it's important to be transparent about how you developed these skills independently of any confidential projects. Discuss your overall industry experience, specific projects that contributed to your skill set, and continuous professional development, without tying any particular technique to the confidential information. This way, you can articulate your competencies without fear of legal repercussions, as long as you're respecting the confidentiality agreement in place. Always focus on your generalized knowledge base and how you have repeatedly refined your practices across various projects.",
